      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## **Introduction**\n",
        "\n",
        "A Variational Autoencoder (VAE) is a generative deep learning model that learns a compact representation of data in a latent space. It consists of two main parts: an encoder and a decoder.\n",
        "\n",
        "The encoder converts an input MNIST image into a smaller latent representation, while the decoder reconstructs the image from this latent representation.\n",
        "\n",
        "In this assignment, the VAE developed in Assignment 8 is used to study its practical applications in compression and denoising. An MNIST image has 28 × 28 pixels, which gives 784 pixel values. The VAE compresses this information into a smaller latent space.\n",
        "\n",
        "The assignment first studies compression using a 2-dimensional latent space. Then, 10 test images are reconstructed and their reconstruction error is calculated using Mean Squared Error (MSE). Gaussian noise is added to 10 images to study the denoising capability of the VAE.\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, the latent dimension is increased from 2 to 16 and 32 to observe how the latent-space size affects compression ratio and reconstruction quality."
      ],
